            "new_string": "---\n\n## 13. Ecosystem Alignment & Prior Art\n\nThe proposed Agent Memory system aligns with emerging standards for persistent agent context in the broader ecosystem.\n\n### Industry Parallels\n*   **Google Memory Bank**: Similar to our \"Lessons and Experiences\" model, [Google's Memory Bank](https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/scale/memory-bank) provides a substrate for agents to store and retrieve long-term facts and procedural trajectories to improve multi-turn consistency.\n*   **Codex Chronicle**: OpenAI's [Codex Chronicle](https://developers.openai.com/codex/memories/chronicle) utilizes a similar \"episodic-to-semantic\" transition, where raw session data is eventually distilled into durable chronicle entries.\n\n### Prototypes and Bridging\nWhile the full Experience layer is being developed, we can **prototype or \"fake\" the procedural recall** by utilizing the existing `entire recall` skill. This allows the agent to manually fetch relevant trajectories or related documentation via a tool-call until the automated injection scoring is fully established in `memory.db`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Decision Points for Code Owners\n",
